{%- comment -%}
  Cart drawer — slides in from the right after an add, so the shopper stays on
  the product or collection page instead of being thrown to /cart.

  The theme's product form is a native {% form 'product' %}, which POSTs and
  lets Shopify redirect to the cart page. app.js intercepts that submit, posts
  to /cart/add.js instead and opens this panel; without JS the form still
  submits normally and the cart page still works, so nothing is lost.

  Rendered inside overlay-group, so it exists on every template. Contents are
  re-rendered through the Section Rendering API — app.js fetches
  ?section_id=cart-drawer and swaps [data-cd-body] only, which is why the panel
  chrome and the scrim sit outside that element. Styles live in theme.css
  rather than here for the same reason: a <style> block inside the swapped
  region would be re-injected on every refresh.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  # One number, in Theme settings › Delivery, instead of the 15000 that used
  # to be written into this file and the copy of it in the other cart
  # surface — and into sixteen sentences that quoted it in prose.
  assign free_ship_threshold = settings.free_shipping_threshold | default: 250 | times: 100
  assign remaining = free_ship_threshold | minus: cart.total_price
  if cart.total_price >= free_ship_threshold
    assign ship_pct = 100
  else
    assign ship_pct = cart.total_price | times: 100 | divided_by: free_ship_threshold
  endif
-%}

<div class="cart-drawer" id="cartDrawer" hidden>
  <div class="cd-scrim" data-cd-close></div>
  <aside class="cd-panel" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-label="Shopping cart" tabindex="-1">
    <header class="cd-head">
      <span class="cd-title">Your Bag{% if cart.item_count > 0 %} <b>({{ cart.item_count }})</b>{% endif %}</span>
      <button type="button" class="cd-close" data-cd-close aria-label="Close cart"><span class="mi" aria-hidden="true">close</span></button>
    </header>

    <div class="cd-body" data-cd-body>
      {%- if cart.item_count > 0 -%}
        {%- comment -%} Free-delivery progress, same threshold as the cart page. {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="cd-ship">
          {%- if cart.total_price >= free_ship_threshold -%}
            <span class="cd-ship-msg is-met"><span class="mi" aria-hidden="true">local_shipping</span>You've unlocked free UAE delivery</span>
          {%- else -%}
            <span class="cd-ship-msg">You’re <b>{{ remaining | money_with_currency }}</b> away from free UAE delivery</span>
          {%- endif -%}
          <span class="cd-ship-bar"><i style="width:{{ ship_pct }}%"></i></span>
        </div>

        <div class="cd-lines">
          {%- for item in cart.items -%}
            <div class="co-line" data-key="{{ item.key }}" data-qty="{{ item.quantity }}">
              {%- if item.image -%}
                <a href="{{ item.url }}" class="cl-img"><img src="{{ item.image | image_url: width: 160 }}" alt="{{ item.title | escape }}" width="80" height="80" loading="lazy"></a>
              {%- endif -%}
              <div class="cl-body">
                <div class="cl-name"><a href="{{ item.url }}">{{ item.product.title }}</a></div>
                {%- comment -%}
                  Line-item properties, inside .cl-meta rather than beside it.
                  A Custom Mixed Spray line reads "100ml / Extrait" and nothing
                  else without them — the oil it is blended from is a property,
                  so unrendered means the shopper cannot check what they
                  ordered. They sit inside the meta div because .cl-body is
                  display:contents in the cart page's grid, so a sibling would
                  become an unplaced grid item and shove the quantity and price
                  rows around.

                  Shopify's convention: a key beginning _ is private to the
                  theme, and a blank value means the field went unfilled.
                {%- endcomment -%}
                <div class="cl-meta">{% unless item.variant.title == 'Default Title' %}{{ item.variant.title }}{% endunless %}{% if item.product.vendor %} · {{ item.product.vendor }}{% endif %}
                  {%- for prop in item.properties -%}
                    {%- unless prop.first == blank or prop.last == blank -%}
                      {%- if prop.first[0] != '_' -%}
                        <span class="cl-prop"><span>{{ prop.first }}</span> {{ prop.last }}</span>
                      {%- endif -%}
                    {%- endunless -%}
                  {%- endfor -%}
                </div>

                <div class="qty-wrap">
                  <button type="button" class="qty-btn" data-cart-step="-1" aria-label="Decrease quantity">&minus;</button>
                  <input class="qty-num" type="text" aria-label="Quantity for {{ item.product.title | escape }}" value="{{ item.quantity }}" readonly>
                  <button type="button" class="qty-btn" data-cart-step="1" aria-label="Increase quantity">+</button>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="cl-price" data-line-price>{{ item.final_line_price | money_with_currency }}</div>
              <button type="button" class="cart-remove" aria-label="Remove {{ item.product.title | escape }}" data-cart-remove><span class="mi" aria-hidden="true">close</span></button>
            </div>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </div>
      {%- else -%}
        <div class="cd-empty">
          <div class="we-ic"><span class="mi" aria-hidden="true">shopping_bag</span></div>
          <h3>Your bag is empty</h3>
          <p>Browse the collection and add something you love.</p>
          <a class="btn-g" href="{{ routes.all_products_collection_url }}" data-cd-close><span class="mi" aria-hidden="true">storefront</span>Continue Shopping</a>
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    {%- if cart.item_count > 0 -%}
      <footer class="cd-foot">
        {% render 'cashback-offer' %}
        {% render 'welcome-offer', style: 'row' %}
        {%- comment -%}
          Collapsed by default — see the snippet for why an open, empty code
          box sends shoppers off the site looking for something to put in it.
          Above the totals, because that is where the discount it produces
          will appear.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {% render 'cart-coupon', uid: 'drawer' %}
        {%- comment -%}
          With a discount on the bag the single Subtotal line was a lie by
          omission: it showed the discounted figure with nothing to say why it
          differed from the prices above it. Before-price, named discounts,
          then the real total.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if cart.total_discount > 0 -%}
          <div class="cd-sub cd-sub--was"><span>Subtotal</span><span>{{ cart.original_total_price | money_with_currency }}</span></div>
          {% render 'cart-discounts', row_class: 'cd-sub cd-sub--disc' %}
          <div class="cd-sub"><span>Total</span><b>{{ cart.total_price | money_with_currency }}</b></div>
        {%- else -%}
          <div class="cd-sub"><span>Subtotal</span><b>{{ cart.total_price | money_with_currency }}</b></div>
        {%- endif -%}
        <p class="cd-note">Taxes and delivery calculated at checkout.</p>
        {%- comment -%}
          "Buy" leaves for the real checkout — the one place a full-page
          handover is what the shopper wants.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <form action="{{ routes.cart_url }}" method="post">
          <button type="submit" name="checkout" class="btn-g cd-checkout"><span class="mi" aria-hidden="true">lock</span>Checkout</button>
        </form>
        {%- comment -%}
          compact: the drawer already carries the free-delivery bar above the
          lines, so it takes the returns link, the security line and the
          WhatsApp contact without repeating an arrival date in a panel this
          narrow. The cart page, which has the room, shows all four.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {% render 'checkout-reassurance', uid: 'drawer', compact: true %}
        <a class="cd-viewcart" href="{{ routes.cart_url }}">View full cart</a>
      </footer>
    {%- endif -%}
  </aside>
</div>

{% schema %}
{ "name": "Cart drawer", "settings": [] }
{% endschema %}
